Idle Balance Activation Agent
5. What is the opportunity that you wish to address?
Many OCBC customers keep large balances sitting for extended periods in regular savings or current accounts with low interest rates, even though these funds are effectively idle — not being used for routine transactions — and could be moved into more profitable products such as time deposits, online savings plans, or mutual funds. Currently, there is no automated mechanism to systematically detect this "idle fund" pattern — RMs only notice it if they happen to review that customer's portfolio manually, or the customer eventually realizes it themselves, often much later. As a result, cross-sell opportunities for funding products are lost, and the bank misses the chance to optimize third-party funds (DPK) that are already within its own customer base. The target segment is retail and premier banking customers whose balance exceeds a certain threshold and whose transaction patterns indicate the funds are not being actively used.
6. What is the proposed solution?
An agentic AI that continuously monitors customer balances and transaction patterns to detect "idle balance" — for example, a consistently high balance with minimal or no significant inflow/outflow activity over a defined period. The system calculates a fit score for how well-suited the customer is to specific funding products (time deposit, online savings plan, or investment products aligned with the customer's risk profile, based on available internal data), then automatically triggers a personalized notification directly through OCBC Mobile, complete with a simulation of the potential returns the customer could gain by reallocating part of their funds — without needing to wait for manual RM follow-up. For high-value customers (premier/priority banking) with large idle balances, the system escalates to the RM as an additional channel for a personal approach. After implementation, funds that were previously sitting idle in low-interest accounts can be converted into more profitable funding products for both the customer and the bank, without RMs having to manually screen through customer portfolios one by one. This agent is designed as an initial foundation — its architecture can be extended into an orchestrator that coordinates other sub-agents, such as churn risk prediction and dynamic rate personalization, in later phases, forming a holistic understanding of each customer's financial health.
7. Rank the business outcomes:
Increase revenue (converting idle funds into higher-margin funding products)
Increase operational efficiency (automated in-app notifications, RM involvement limited to high-value cases)
Improve customer experience (proactive, relevant recommendations without waiting on RM follow-up)
Reduce cost
Reduce risk or compliance lapses